  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan returnees from Iran Acute Crisis Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IRC and AABRAR lead an integrated health and protection intervention, targeting 33,003 people.  15,263 in health and 17,740 in protection in Islam Qala and Herat city. Under health, IRC will provide comprehensive PHC services including 12,186 PHC consultations (CDs, NCDs, SRH, injuries, vaccination, S-GBV) and 2,437 MH consultations as per national guidelines. AABRAR will complement with 640 medical assistive devices for PWD. The proposed interventions will complement the ongoing IRC health/nutrition services and UNFPA, WHO, World Vision services.  IRC and AABRAR address protection risks faced by 6640 returnees at the Zero Point in Islam Qala, and in Herat city. AABRAR will support 700 PWDs through transportation, implement PWD accessibility interventions (e.g. ramps, handrails) reaching 1800 people, provide repairs of prostheses (800 returnees) and install accessible signage boards (3,000 returnees). AABRAR will support a total of 6,300 returnees. IRC will provide IPA for 340 people (Up to 120$ case-by-case) and support for 100 UASC (transportation, accommodation, and documentation). Protection monitoring, safe referral and information will be provided on legal documentation, reaching 11,000 people. IRC/AABRAR will coordinate with other JR members, including SCI, War child and Care for referrals for PWD to AABRAR. Protection mainstreaming is done through training frontline workers on protection, PSEA and safeguarding.</narrative>
  </description>
